      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we first need to determine the prime factorizations of both numbers.\n\nThe prime factorization of 12 is:\n\\[ 12 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 = 2^2 \\times 3 \\]\n\nThe prime factorization of 20 is:\n\\[ 20 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 5 = 2^2 \\times 5 \\]\n\nThe GCD is found by taking the lowest power of each prime factor that appears in both factorizations. Here, the only common prime factor is 2, and the lowest power of 2 that appears in both factorizations is \\(2^2 = 4\\).\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
